    "narrative": "The offensive core for Ghost Ride the WHIP tonight centers on **Isaac Paredes** and **Brice Turang**, our two highest-rated starters. **Isaac Paredes** leads the group with a 66.57 efficiency score, fueled by a favorable 4.64 xERA matchup against Grayson Rodriguez and a significant boost from his #3 spot in the order. **Brice Turang** earns high marks at 63.14; while he faces a solid arm in Kirby, the lead-off designation provides the volume necessary to hunt for the stolen bases that remain our primary catalyst in the 5x5 standings. **Max Muncy** rounds out our top-tier plays at 62.02, as his power profile aligns well against Dobnak\u2019s 4.70 xERA, offering a strong floor for both R and RBI categories.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision landed on the bench, where **Vinnie Pasquantino** just missed the cut. While he possesses the talent to start, his 48.79 score was suppressed by a poor platoon match against the southpaw Jump, forcing us to prioritize the higher-ceiling utility profiles of **Austin Riley** and **Jose Caballero**. Though **Jose Caballero** is mired in the #9 spot today, his elite sprint speed makes him an essential \"keep\" in the lineup despite the -8% penalty for his position in the order. Conversely, **Josh Naylor** and **Travis Bazzana** both hover in the 55-range, showing enough stability to warrant starts, but we must monitor the late-afternoon weather reports for any developments that could compromise their efficiency. With **James Wood** still sidelined on the IL, our depth is currently tested, making the consistent production of this starting seven critical to protecting our league standing.",
